From: Wayland Cursor Fix <local@localhost>
Date: Mon, 03 Aug 2026 22:05:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] xwayland: WCF_DEBUG release-path diagnostics

Optional runtime logging for diagnosis of grab->ungrab restore failures
on real game sessions. Set WCF_DEBUG=1 for journal output or
WCF_DEBUG=/path/to/file to also append to a file. No behavioral change
with the variable unset.

Logs: pointer enter/leave (+grab state), hidden-cursor lock decisions,
lock engage/unlock events, release-candidate set/invalidate (with
timestamp gaps), release-branch entry/skip/decision (candidate vs
fallback + coords), unlock-hint commits, pointer-warp-v1 sends or guard
drops (missing serial/caps/focus, out-of-bounds target), and the first
absolute pointer motion (position + delay) after each accepted warp_v1,
to expose stale absolute events overwriting a restore.
---
 hw/xwayland/xwayland-input.c | 115 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 1 file changed, 

--- a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-input.c
+++ b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-input.c
@@ -57,6 +57,8 @@
 #include "xwayland-keyboard-grab-unstable-v1-client-protocol.h"
 #include "keyboard-shortcuts-inhibit-unstable-v1-client-protocol.h"
 
